{
  "requirement": "The SDK supplies the inspection tools described in\n[Validation context](validation-context.md). Graph tools invoke the application's graph\nand contents interfaces; source tools invoke its source interfaces and\nsource-node mapping.\n\nThe SDK defines the built-in tools and their input-recording policy.\n`read_node` accepts every domain node kind.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no adequacy gap. I mapped each obligation in `fixed_tools` to the supplied tests below.\n\n**Built-in tools are supplied.**\n- The graph-only tool set is asserted by name and order in `agent/tests.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]`. The set is `read_node`, `outgoing_edges`, `get_next_page` and `submit_result`.\n- That test also asserts the `get_next_page` and `submit_result` schemas.\n- The tool set in `configured.rs#fn[supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport]` is asserted on the wire for all four requests.\n- With sources attached, `configured.rs#fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]` asserts the full list. It adds `list_sources`, `outline_source`, `search_text`, `search_structure` and `finish_search`. It also asserts that `node` is an integer parameter for `read_node`, `outline_source` and `outgoing_edges`.\n- The `read_source` tool is not in that attached-sources list. It is exercised directly in `agent/tests.rs#fn[source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results]`.\n\n**Graph tools invoke the application's graph and contents interfaces.**\n- `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` checks that `outgoing_edges` returns the domain's edge targets `[3,2,3]`. It also checks that the domain is queried once, and not relisted.\n- `graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery` and `queued_contents_and_graph_read_tools_redact_credentials_before_delivery` check that `read_node` returns the domain's node content.\n\n**Source tools invoke the source interfaces and source-node mapping.**\n- `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results` uses a recording `SourceProvider`. It asserts the exact forwarded arguments for `list_sources`, `search_text` and `search_structure`: prefix, context, limit, rule and language. It asserts the presented results and that provider errors surface. It also asserts that `outline_source` and `read_source` go through the observation (mapping) callback with the right selectors. Discovery tools record no dependency.\n- `configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions` runs against real disk sources. It checks that `list_sources` entries carry integer node IDs and that a bad node ID is rejected. It checks that a mapped source node reads as the domain's snapshot text and not the disk contents. It also checks the recorded dependencies, including the mapped-source fingerprints, and the `finish_search` behaviour.\n- `agent/project_sources.rs#fn[structural_tags_select_only_the_original_enclosing_item]` and `#fn[outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items]` cover structural search, the outline, and `read_node` on source children, including dependency recording.\n\n**Input-recording policy.**\n- A delivered `read_node` or `outgoing_edges` call is recorded as a dependency.\n- A failed delivery is not recorded. This is asserted in `graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery` and in the \"prepared selection is not an input until delivery succeeds\" part of `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets`.\n- A malformed node ID records nothing and does not query the graph.\n- Search discovery records nothing. `finish_search` records only the selected hits. The structural-search test asserts this with the fingerprint taken before the file changed.\n\n**`read_node` accepts every domain node kind.**\n- `configured.rs#fn[read_node_advertises_and_reads_every_domain_id_variant]` uses a domain with two node-data variants, `LookupNode::Requirement` and `LookupNode::Selection`. It checks that `read_node` reads both through the `read_node` tool. It asserts the exact returned text, the recorded dependencies, and the integer `node` schema.\n- Source nodes are covered by the mapped-source read in the configured-agent test.\n\nThere are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments and no unresolved ambiguities. The `{impl}` site is `agent/tools.rs#impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[tools]`. It builds the tool definitions that these tests assert.",
  "references": "bc01efa0565e9fb481949e7475adbab678db951ee8f8fea9d17e39d096a596e9",
